// A swing is a commitment, and this is what makes it one.
//
// Four presses: ticks 0, 5, 19 and 20. The ones at 5 and 19 land during the
// swing and must be **dropped** — not queued, not stacked. Without that,
// holding the button is strictly better than timing it, and recovery stops
// meaning anything.
//
// **The press at 19 is the one that pins the length**, and it is here because
// the first version of this file was missing it. SWING is
// STARTUP + ACTIVE + RECOVERY = 6 + 4 + 10 = 20 ticks, running on ticks 0
// through 19, so 19 is the last tick that must refuse a press and 20 is the
// first that must accept one. Testing only 20 pins the swing from one side:
// shortening RECOVERY to 9 ends the swing after tick 18, tick 20 is still free,
// and the trace comes out identical. That mutation escaped.
//
// With both ticks pressed the number is pinned from both sides. A shorter swing
// accepts 19 and the second `swung` moves; a longer one refuses 20 and the
// second `swung` disappears.
//
// Buffering that dropped press is a real feature and a deliberately separate
// one: it needs an expiry and a rule about which phase accepts it, and guessing
// those before there is an animation to feel them against would bake in a
// decision nobody has tested.
//
// No bodies at all — this is about the state machine, and a target would only
// add contact events to the trace.
(
    description: "A press during a swing is dropped; the next one is accepted exactly when recovery ends.",
    setup: (),
    inputs: [],
    attacks: [0, 5, 19, 20],
    budget: (ticks: 45),
    expect: (
        struck: 0,
        hitbox: false,
        enemy_count: 0,
        trace: "a_press_during_a_swing_is_dropped.trace",
    ),
)
